# SQL's `project *` alone: DS0117 with a fix that removes the step.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | project * | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..39
  PIPELINE@0..38
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    PROJECT_OP@20..29
      IDENT@20..27 "project"
      WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
      ERROR@28..29
        STAR@28..29 "*"
    WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
    PIPE@30..31 "|"
    WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
    TAKE_OP@32..38
      IDENT@32..36 "take"
      WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
      LITERAL@37..38
        LONG@37..38 "5"
  WHITESPACE@38..39 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `project *` is SQL's `SELECT *`
  --> query:1:29
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | project * | take 5
  |                             ^ `project` lists the columns to keep
  |
  = help: every column is kept already: remove `| project *`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | take 5
which parses without errors
